  ▐ aura  Wrote it — `answer.md`, Day 4, under 400 words, nothing else touched.

Elias's Sunday: he breaks the pattern before it breaks him. Instead of choosing between the frost money and Mare's "we arrive together," he puts her in the passenger seat — literally, torch in hand, walking into Pat's at ten past one as a pair. Callum gets a time plus terms (beers after pudding, money-talk Monday). Pat gets told the table doesn't split. And the centerpiece: at two, in Tom's chair, Elias says out loud — for the first time in twenty years — *"Dad sat here. Nobody ever says it. I miss him — and I hate how he taught us all to be fluent in silence."*

Feelings tracked against his week: sadness finally moves (7, as he predicted Saturday), fear drops to 4, affection climbs to 8, happiness hits a personal-best 6. Anger and disgust stay near-absent, consistent with the ground logs [2b4fcb370cd6, ac7a5f8a1da2, ef1458190cf7, 2e9fab402445, f22b404402c3]. And he names the one seed that says he doesn't steer toward repair [8583374323e5] — today's the day he tests it with gravy.
